<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tondaimandalam</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tondai Nadu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tondaimandalam is a historical region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a> and southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanchipuram">Kanchipuram</a> and including the area of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chennai">Chennai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vellore">Vellore</a>. It was the heartland of the Pallava dynasty from the fourth to the ninth century and was annexed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> around 900, under whom it was known as Jayankonda Cholamandalam.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tondaimandalam.jpg" alt="Tondaimandalam" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nesa raja sekaran · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tondai_Nadu_AP%2BTN_(NRS).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
